<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Friday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p> B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p> C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p> E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p> F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p> G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p> H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*  *G*   *H*</p>
<p>Jan 17  20,470 4,457 24,927 13,606 13,651 5,293  0  19,203</p>
<p>Jan 20  20,477 4,457 24,934 13,597 13,607 5,338  0  19,204</p>
<p>Jan 21  20,431 4,599 25,030 13,431 13,437 5,478  0  19,174</p>
<p>Jan 22  20,524 4,690 25,214 13,284 13,288 5,730  0  19,261</p>
<p>Jan 23  20,554 4,668 25,222 13,176 13,180 5,864  0  19,273</p>
<p>Jan 24  20,498 4,563 25,061 13,048 13,056 5,936  0  19,211</p>
<p>Jan 27  20,607 4,465 25,072 12,989 12,993 6,112  0  19,304</p>
<p>Jan 28  20,597 4,370 24,967 12,931 12,935 6,169  0  19,303</p>
<p>Jan 29  20,182 4,276 24,458 12,927 12,930 5,971  0  18,901</p>
<p>*A  Of the $20.18 billion in international reserves, $2.42 billion (11.98 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>(( - Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0651))</p>
</text>
